Add optional profileIndex to the termEntries API path

Upstream `termEntries` always resolves against `optionsFull.profileCurrent`, so an
external client cannot choose which Yomitan profile a lookup runs against. For a
multi-language client this means a lookup cannot be directed at the right language:
a profile configured for Japanese will not deinflect "running" into "run".

This mirrors the existing `ankiCardFormats` case in the same switch block, which
already accepts an optional `profileIndex` and falls back to the current profile,
so the request shape and the fallback behaviour stay consistent across paths.
Omitting `profileIndex` preserves the current behaviour exactly.

File: ext/js/comm/yomitan-api.js

--- a/ext/js/comm/yomitan-api.js
+++ b/ext/js/comm/yomitan-api.js
@@ -165,26 +165,32 @@
                     case 'termEntries': {
                         /** @type {import('yomitan-api.js').termEntriesInput} */
                         // @ts-expect-error - Allow this to error
-                        const {term} = parsedBody;
+                        const {term, profileIndex} = parsedBody;
+                        const resolvedProfileIndex = typeof profileIndex === 'number' ? profileIndex : optionsFull.profileCurrent;
+                        if (typeof optionsFull.profiles[resolvedProfileIndex] === 'undefined') {
+                            throw new Error('Invalid input for termEntries, expected "profileIndex" to be a valid profile index but got ' + profileIndex);
+                        }
                         if (typeof term === 'string') {
                             const invokeParams = {
                                 text: term,
                                 details: {},
-                                optionsContext: {index: optionsFull.profileCurrent},
+                                optionsContext: {index: resolvedProfileIndex},
                             };
                             result = {...await this._invoke('termsFind', invokeParams), index: 0};
                         } else if (Array.isArray(term)) {
                             result = await Promise.all(term.map(async (text, index) => {
                                 const invokeParams = {
                                     text,
                                     details: {},
-                                    optionsContext: {index: optionsFull.profileCurrent},
+                                    optionsContext: {index: resolvedProfileIndex},
                                 };
                                 return {
                                     ...(await this._invoke('termsFind', invokeParams)),
                                     index,
                                 };
                             }));
                         } else {
                             throw new Error('Invalid input for termEntries, expected "term" to be a string or a string array but got ' + typeof term);
                         }
                         break;
                     }

Also update the input type in types/ext/yomitan-api.d.ts:

    termEntriesInput: {
        term: string | string[];
        profileIndex?: number;
    }

And docs/api_paths/termEntries.md in yomidevs/yomitan-api, adding to Request Options:

    - `profileIndex` (`number`): (Optional) The index of the Yomitan profile to look
      the term up against. Defaults to the currently active profile.

`ankiFields` needs the same treatment, and for the same reason. A client that
resolves a term against profile 1 and then renders it through `ankiFields` gets the
glossary for whatever profile happens to be active, so a correct English definition
is replaced a moment later by a Japanese one. Observed in practice before this hunk
was added.

--- a/ext/js/comm/yomitan-api.js
+++ b/ext/js/comm/yomitan-api.js
@@ -212,10 +212,14 @@
                     case 'ankiFields': {
-                        const {text, type, markers, maxEntries, includeMedia} = parsedBody;
+                        const {text, type, markers, maxEntries, includeMedia, profileIndex} = parsedBody;
                         const includeAudioMedia = includeMedia && markers.includes('audio');
 
-                        const profileOptions = optionsFull.profiles[optionsFull.profileCurrent].options;
+                        const ankiFieldsProfileIndex = typeof profileIndex === 'number' ? profileIndex : optionsFull.profileCurrent;
+                        if (typeof optionsFull.profiles[ankiFieldsProfileIndex] === 'undefined') {
+                            throw new Error('Invalid input for ankiFields, expected "profileIndex" to be a valid profile index but got ' + profileIndex);
+                        }
+                        const profileOptions = optionsFull.profiles[ankiFieldsProfileIndex].options;
 
                         const ankiTemplate = await this._getAnkiTemplate(profileOptions);
-                        let dictionaryEntries = await this._getDictionaryEntries(text, type, optionsFull.profileCurrent);
+                        let dictionaryEntries = await this._getDictionaryEntries(text, type, ankiFieldsProfileIndex);

And in types/ext/yomitan-api.d.ts, ankiFieldsInput gains `profileIndex?: number;`.

Note: `kanjiEntries` still hardcodes `optionsFull.profileCurrent`. It is untouched here
only because the tool does not yet call it; the same fix applies.

Verification (requires a browser with Yomitan running and the API enabled):

    curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:19633/termEntries \
      -d '{"term":"corriendo","profileIndex":2}' | head -c 400

Against a Spanish profile this should resolve to "correr"; against the Japanese
profile at index 0 it should return no entries. If both return the same result,
the patch is not loaded.
